  "implementation": {
    "provider": "After a vetoed local textarea proposal, a changed focused canonical model completes the original NSTextView scrollRangeToVisible method. Unchanged cancellation clears the pending reveal; unrelated programmatic changes do not inherit it. No UI/layout/scroll calculation or API extension.",
    "firefox": "Keep the live owned image and cached clip geometry during reentrant engine pre-edit callbacks. Avoid rebinding an intentionally busy native editor. Post-key canonical sync echoes the native viewport through the existing Gecko scroll setter.",
    "chromium": "Keep native geometry/read-only image during reentrant Blink callbacks, then return the post-key native viewport through the existing engine setter after canonical model sync.",
    "coordinates": "Use original LocalFrameView::ConvertFromRootFrame with the element client quads. The previous RootFrameToDocument incorrectly added the page scroll to native-local pointer input. Exact call bytes guarded; no copied coordinate/scroll algorithm.",
    "scope": "Exact pinned unchanged Debian ARM64 Chromium and Firefox, software/headless Wayland, 100 percent scale. Native default vertical/wrapped textareas; opt-in, not installed as the desktop default."
  },
